; ============================================================
; THE BYZANTINE SHADOW
; MODULE 04 -- CONSTRUCTION
; ============================================================
;
; Construction authority / executor v0.1
;
; PURPOSE
;   Own basic building construction decisions and execution.
;
; CURRENT SCOPE
;   - Housing maintenance
;   - Barracks establishment
;   - Basic construction verification
;
; SHADOW-DERIVED PRINCIPLES
;   1. A build predicate is not completion evidence.
;   2. Pending construction must suppress duplicate commands.
;   3. Existing world state is authoritative for completion.
;   4. Construction execution is distinct from strategic intent.
;   5. This module must not manufacture strategic objectives.
;
; CURRENT LIMITATION
;   The complete Shadow construction state machine has not yet
;   been transplanted. In particular, the canonical ABI for:
;
;       gl-current-build-item
;       gl-progression-pause
;       up-assign-builders
;       place-control
;
;   remains pending canonical-source extraction.
;
;   Therefore this module deliberately implements only the
;   construction behavior whose predicates and executor forms
;   are already established in the current project.
;
; EXECUTION MODEL
;
;       WORLD OBSERVATION
;              |
;              v
;       CONSTRUCTION NEED
;              |
;              v
;       FEASIBILITY
;              |
;              v
;       PENDING GUARD
;              |
;              v
;       BUILD COMMAND
;              |
;              v
;       WORLD-STATE VERIFICATION
;
; IMPORTANT
;   Issuing (build X) is NOT proof that X exists.
;
; ============================================================


; ============================================================
; HOUSING
; ============================================================
;
; Maintain housing before the population reaches a hard stop.
;
; Shadow-compatible guards:
;   - house headroom
;   - population headroom
;   - can-build
;   - pending-object suppression
;
; The pending-object guard prevents repeated house commands
; while an existing house foundation is already pending.
;
; ============================================================

(defrule
    (house-headroom < 5)
    (population-headroom != 0)
    (can-build house)
    (up-pending-objects c: house < 1)
=>
    (build house)
)


; ============================================================
; BARRACKS -- INITIAL ESTABLISHMENT
; ============================================================
;
; A barracks is required before the basic military layer can
; become operational.
;
; BASIC-BARRACKS-READY is produced by Module 02 from observed
; barracks world state.
;
; Construction therefore consumes the state rather than
; independently declaring the barracks ready.
;
; ============================================================

(defrule
    (goal BASIC-BARRACKS-READY 0)
    (can-build barracks)
    (up-pending-objects c: barracks < 1)
=>
    (build barracks)
)


; ============================================================
; BARRACKS -- DUPLICATE COMMAND SUPPRESSION
; ============================================================
;
; If a barracks already exists, no construction command is
; necessary.
;
; This rule intentionally has no action.
;
; World-state observation remains owned by Module 02.
;
; ============================================================

(defrule
    (building-type-count-total barracks > 0)
=>
    (disable-self)
)


; ============================================================
; BASIC CONSTRUCTION SAFETY
; ============================================================
;
; Do not issue another barracks command while a barracks
; foundation/object is already pending.
;
; This is deliberately kept separate from completion.
;
; up-pending-objects answers whether the engine reports a
; pending object; building-type-count-total answers whether
; the completed/recognized building population exists.
;
; They must not be treated as interchangeable.
;
; ============================================================

(defrule
    (building-type-count-total barracks < 1)
    (up-pending-objects c: barracks >= 1)
=>
    (disable-self)
)


; ============================================================
; FARM CONSTRUCTION -- BASIC FOOD INFRASTRUCTURE
; ============================================================
;
; Conservative Shadow-derived farm rule.
;
; This is intentionally NOT the complete Shadow farm state
; machine. The canonical source contains substantially richer
; farm arbitration involving:
;
;   gl-current-build-item
;   gl-build-progress
;   SPLIT
;   escrow state
;   pending objects
;   strategic conditions
;   normal placement
;
; Until that ABI is fully recovered and registered, only the
; basic pending-object / world-state relationship is installed.
;
; ============================================================

(defrule
    (can-build farm)
    (up-pending-objects c: farm < 1)
    (building-type-count-total farm < 50)
    (wood-amount >= 60)
=>
    (build farm)
)


; ============================================================
; CONSTRUCTION TERMINAL OBSERVATION
; ============================================================
;
; These rules do not issue construction commands.
;
; They exist to expose basic world-state consequences to the
; already-existing state layer.
;
; Module 02 remains responsible for BASIC-BARRACKS-READY.
;
; ============================================================

(defrule
    (building-type-count-total barracks > 0)
=>
    (set-goal BASIC-BARRACKS-READY 1)
    (set-goal BASIC-ATTACK-READY 1)
)


(defrule
    (building-type-count-total barracks < 1)
=>
    (set-goal BASIC-BARRACKS-READY 0)
    (set-goal BASIC-ATTACK-READY 0)
)


; ============================================================
; END MODULE 04
; ============================================================